API.md R6, TYPES.md §1: a root broken only by naming a root the checker broke, in another
package, is explained by that root's error; exit 1.
-- args --
explain
y
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

import b

/// Names b's broken value.
let y: Int = b.x + 1
-- b/b.canon --
/// B.
package b

/// A type error.
let x: Int = "s"
-- want --
[exit 1]
[stdout]
error[E3002]  b/b.canon:5:14
  expected Int, found String
[stderr]
canon: y: value could not be computed: root y
